  "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $T:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{4}.$ If $\\text{rank}(T)=4$ then $\\text{nullity}(T)=$",
  "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given transformation, we have $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(T) & =4 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(T) & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
